# ============================================================================
# THE TAU-NOMIC TUTORIAL SERIES - READ ME FIRST
# A living, self-amending constitution, explained in eight runnable files (plus two appendices)
# ============================================================================
#
# WHAT THIS IS
# tau-nomic is a constitution that runs: its laws are first-class values
# of a decidable algebra, it amends itself under an entrenched core, and
# its central guarantee - "no sequence of legal steps ever breaks the
# core" - is not enforced by anyone. It is derived. This series explains
# how, in eight self-contained .tau files. Every claim is a runnable query;
# three parts replay entire constitutional histories by themselves when you
# run the file.
#
# THE PARTS (read in order - each builds on the last)
#   01 specs_as_values      What only Tau can do: specifications as
#                           decidable VALUES (meet, entailment,
#                           self-reference without paradox).
#   02 decide_not_vote      Idempotence: repetition has no weight - why
#                           a deciding kernel has no use for majorities.
#   03 living_constitution  The kernel starts to RUN: law as temporal
#                           state, adopt/reject as arithmetic.
#   04 actions              Judging deeds under the law: a three-valued
#                           verdict (legal / irregular / unconstitutional).
#   05 ratchet              Irreversibility and path-dependence: the
#                           guarantee no other system can give.
#   06 eternity_clause      A real constitution's core (German Basic Law,
#                           Art. 79(3)) mechanized - the Enabling-Act
#                           move becomes a provable rejection.
#   07 the_map              What reduces to SAT (and why that is good),
#                           what is irreplaceable, which query form
#                           scales.
#   08 the_edges            What honestly stays outside: translation,
#                           enforcement, identity, choice - and why
#                           naming the edges is design, not defeat.
#   09 the_full_palette     Appendix: richer rights - scoped, with
#                           exceptions, quantitative (bv thresholds),
#                           temporal ([t-1] inside a right), and one
#                           guarantee over ALL future amendments.
#   10 the_trilemma         Appendix II: who amends the amendment rule?
#                           Tau's u stream (the spec rewrites ITSELF),
#                           a two-step coup, self-binding via `this` -
#                           and the proved trilemma that forces the
#                           fixed-spec + law-as-state architecture.
#
# REQUIREMENTS
#   The Tau Language framework: https://github.com/IDNI/tau-lang
#   This series is verified against: Tau 0.7.0-alpha, build 240788e.
#   (Alpha software - syntax and behavior may drift between builds. If a
#   file misbehaves on a newer build, check the project's release notes.)
#
# HOW TO RUN A PART
#   tau -q < nomic_01_specs_as_values.tau
#
# HOW TO READ THE OUTPUT
#   The REPL echoes every input line, then numbers results as %1, %2, ...
#   Scan for the "%N: ..." lines - each file annotates its expected
#   values inline. In the run-based parts (03-06) look for the
#   "o0res[t] := ..." (verdict codes) and "o0s[t] := ..." (the living
#   law) lines instead; the run prints one large normalized formula
#   first - scan past it. On a POSIX shell:
#     tau -q < file.tau 2>&1 | grep -E '^%[0-9]+:'           (parts 1,2,7,8)
#     tau -q < file.tau 2>&1 | grep -E '^(o0res|o0law|o0seal|o0s)\[' (3-6)
#   Part 10's session prints its own streams: u[k] := F means the step-k
#   proposal was rejected (or none was made); u[k] := a specification
#   means it was adopted.
#
# ONE QUERY TO CHECK YOUR SETUP (expected result: T)

# EXPECTED-RESULTS: T

set charvar off
sat { o1[t]=0 } != 0.
# => %1: T
#    If you see T, your installation works - start with part 01.
#
# ============================================================================
# END - continue with nomic_01_specs_as_values.tau
# ============================================================================
